        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "BRIDGET C. ASAY, ESQ., Assistant Attorney General, Montpelier, Vermont; on behalf of Petitioners."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "EDWIN S. KNEEDLER",
      "case_id": "2010-10-779",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0a0d77f92a05704880b38eb7ccc2a74e76ecabd1f876929da7c579d05bc04e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0a0d77f92a0-0000-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "EDWIN S. KNEEDLER, ESQ., Deputy Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting Petitioners."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "THOMAS C. GOLDSTEIN",
      "case_id": "2010-10-779",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0a0d77f92a05704880b38eb7ccc2a74e76ecabd1f876929da7c579d05bc04e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0a0d77f92a0-0000-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "THOMAS C. GOLDSTEIN, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of Respondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "BRIDGET C. ASAY",
      "case_id": "2010-10-779",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0a0d77f92a05704880b38eb7ccc2a74e76ecabd1f876929da7c579d05bc04e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0a0d77f92a0-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. ASAY: I disagree, Your Honor. The purpose of the statute is to let doctors decide whether sales representatives will have access to this inside information about what they have been prescribing to their patients."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-10-779",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0a0d77f92a05704880b38eb7ccc2a74e76ecabd1f876929da7c579d05bc04e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0a0d77f92a0-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: But they could use it for other purposes, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-10-779",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0a0d77f92a05704880b38eb7ccc2a74e76ecabd1f876929da7c579d05bc04e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0a0d77f92a0-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Could you please -- could you please answer yes or no? If you're changing your position, you're changing your position."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Asay",
      "case_id": "2010-10-779",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0a0d77f92a05704880b38eb7ccc2a74e76ecabd1f876929da7c579d05bc04e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0a0d77f92a0-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We interpret the first clause of the statute to be a restriction on sale, except for sale for the exemptions that are set forth in the statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2010-10-779",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0a0d77f92a05704880b38eb7ccc2a74e76ecabd1f876929da7c579d05bc04e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0a0d77f92a0-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And could you explain how you're going to interpret your statute going forward and apply your statute going forward?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Edwin S. Kneedler",
      "case_id": "2010-10-779",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0a0d77f92a05704880b38eb7ccc2a74e76ecabd1f876929da7c579d05bc04e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0a0d77f92a0-0001-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Vermont statute protects important interests that the Vermont legislature could recognize in physician autonomy and control over information that concerns them."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-10-779",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0a0d77f92a05704880b38eb7ccc2a74e76ecabd1f876929da7c579d05bc04e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0a0d77f92a0-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All right, so long as I know that's what you're talking about. When you say \"privacy,\" you don't mean the prescriber's concern that people will know that he prescribed certain drugs."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2010-10-779",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0a0d77f92a05704880b38eb7ccc2a74e76ecabd1f876929da7c579d05bc04e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0a0d77f92a0-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But there is another interest here besides the State's concern about health care costs, and that is the physician's privacy interests."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-10-779",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0a0d77f92a05704880b38eb7ccc2a74e76ecabd1f876929da7c579d05bc04e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0a0d77f92a0-0002-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The State sought to ensure costs are contained in the private health care sector, as well as for State purchasers of prescription drugs, through the promotion of less costly drugs and ensuring prescribers received unbiased information."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Vermont",
      "case_id": "2010-10-779",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0a0d77f92a05704880b38eb7ccc2a74e76ecabd1f876929da7c579d05bc04e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0a0d77f92a0-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If Vermont were serious about protecting the doctors' privacy, as opposed to kind of a, a right of publicity, a control over information about them, it wouldn't have all these exemptions; it would have a provision that says this is private information."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2010-10-779",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0a0d77f92a05704880b38eb7ccc2a74e76ecabd1f876929da7c579d05bc04e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0a0d77f92a0-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Does the Constitution of the United States forbid them, having made those findings in detail, from controlling advertising to prevent what they have determined is a false and misleading practice?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SOTOMAYOR",
      "case_id": "2010-10-779",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0a0d77f92a05704880b38eb7ccc2a74e76ecabd1f876929da7c579d05bc04e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0a0d77f92a0-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I have a difficulty. Today with the Internet and with computers, there's virtually no privacy individuals have."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "National Association of Chain Drugstores",
      "case_id": "2010-10-779",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0a0d77f92a05704880b38eb7ccc2a74e76ecabd1f876929da7c579d05bc04e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0a0d77f92a0-0002-0005",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I would direct you to the amicus brief -- you don't have to pull it out right now, but for later. The brief of the National Association of Chain Drugstores, if you just make a reference, on pages 10 to 11 collects the history of how this information has been gathered."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State of Vermont",
      "case_id": "2010-10-779",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0a0d77f92a05704880b38eb7ccc2a74e76ecabd1f876929da7c579d05bc04e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0a0d77f92a0-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the State -- \"the statute's parallel formulary compliance exemption.\" And this paragraph talks about advocacy by the insurance companies."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2010-10-779",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0a0d77f92a05704880b38eb7ccc2a74e76ecabd1f876929da7c579d05bc04e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0a0d77f92a0-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Are you saying that all those should be reexamined?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Asay",
      "case_id": "2010-10-779",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0a0d77f92a05704880b38eb7ccc2a74e76ecabd1f876929da7c579d05bc04e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0a0d77f92a0-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. ASAY: I would like to begin with the point that my friend was making about the use of the information by insurance companies. Insurers are not similarly situated to pharmaceutical manufacturers."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2010-10-779",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0a0d77f92a05704880b38eb7ccc2a74e76ecabd1f876929da7c579d05bc04e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0a0d77f92a0-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Do we have -- were there -- were there findings with respect to the statute as enacted?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2010-10-779",
      "confidence": 0.0,
